Subject: [PATCH] IO-NOGUARD + MT-ENABLE + SR-HANG + OPLOG-3: IO page
 unguarded, Motor Test grid = Mot_Table Enable=1, State Record children
 detached, card errors in the op log
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260929, on the machine:
- "IO畫面一律不要卡控，讓我測試" (after C_Auto2_Up was refused: its Cylinder[] is switched off by golden cinitial.cpp:5296-5304 because
  Gerneral.ini USE_AUTO_RETEST=0, while IO_Table has Enable=1). JsonBridge/IoBtnPanelClick.cpp: #define W906_IO_PAGE_NO_GUARDS 1 --
  every golden rule that greys an IO button is skipped and listed in the reply's guardsBypassed (running/SystemStart, SoftStart,
  IO_Table Enable=0, engine object off, Index-has-IC, EP_Install, the LOAD_Z_USE_MOTOR lanes, and the Index brake release without
  power -- the last one can let a vertical axis sag, EastSun told). Physical limits stay: not a 1203 point, an input, no route.
  tools/wb_serve.cpp: the three dialog wait loops (ShowErrorMessage / YesNo / MyMessageBox) serve io.btnPanelClick while a dialog is
  open when W906_IoPageNoGuards() (was modal-pending). 0 restores golden. Same-line edits.
- "需要你把MOT_Table有 enable 等於1的 才動態顯示在上面 開軟體偵測一次 不要都顯示在上面": JsonBridge/ChanMotorPoints.cpp
  motorTestVisible = Mot_Table Enable=1 (HSys.MotTable, read at start-up; HW.MotorTest.html applyGoldenGridVisibility shows only
  those rows); golden bView kept as goldenMotorTestVisible. This machine: 19 of 48 rows (all PCI1203). tests/test_motor_points.cpp
  checks the new rule on every row and golden's cases on goldenMotorTestVisible.
- State Record froze the whole wb_serve under the F5 debugger (11:26:45: 20 of 22 threads Suspended, F6 pause dead; 1.bat's last
  line `d:\HT9045\7z.exe a -tzip ...Automation\2026_09.7z` stuck at start with 0 ms CPU; the same 7z runs in 47 ms standalone).
  Not reproducible under a command-line gdb --batch (a harness with the same SHFileOperation -> batch -> system(7z) finished), so
  this fixes the environment difference and bounds the wait: cStateRecord.cpp RunStateRecordJob runs the batch and the final zip
  through W906_SrRunAndWait (CREATE_NO_WINDOW = its own hidden console, as golden's GUI parent gave it; no inherited handles; a job
  with KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE; 600 s then TerminateJobObject -- the old system() had no limit), and the worker thread initialises COM
  (STA, ole32 via LoadLibrary) for SHFileOperation / ShellExecute. NOT yet verified on the machine (EastSun: State Record later).
- op log: MOT lines add cardErr / cardErrText (Acm_GetLastError + the vendor's text, e.g. "Positive hardware limit has been
  exceeded") and drvAlm (603Fh); SREC lines trace the State Record worker (g_W906StateRecordNote).
Also found and repaired today (no source change): libht9045_sm.a truncated to 6.5 MB at 11:58:20 by an interrupted F5 pre-launch
build (ar's temp std0vN7B left behind) -> "file too short", wb_serve.exe gone; both deleted, rebuilt (34.1 MB).
Build build_integ_ship_x86 --target wb_serve exit 0; pe_truncation_check 178 complete; the new strings are in wb_serve.exe.
MachineType.h (EastSun's SOFT_SIMULTE edit) is not in this commit.

